  "limitations": [
    "The v2 series has one request per configuration; v1 supplies one repeat but not enough samples for confidence intervals.",
    "Q4_K_M and TQ3_4S generated different response lengths and content, so fixed-slot decode is not an equal-token replay benchmark.",
    "The lexical 4/5 anchor score does not evaluate semantic correctness; this prompt favored Q4_K_M semantically.",
    "moe_decode_miss_rate is the expert-cache L1 miss rate, not prompt/radix-cache or KV-cache miss rate.",
    "Physical NVMe request reads are order- and Linux-page-cache-dependent. The page cache was not forcibly dropped, so these bytes are descriptive rather than a codec-only causal estimate.",
    "BF16 compute is held constant for this A/B but is not native arithmetic on SM75; FP16 remains a separate runtime experiment."
  ],
  "decision": "Keep TQ3_4S as the preferred Ornith weight format for this machine. Its smaller expert records improve fixed-slot throughput and, more importantly, permit 1204 additional expert slots; that capacity cuts deterministic-output expert misses and copy pressure enough to reproduce a large decode gain. Do not claim quality parity from this single task."
